```

New version: after the aggro assertion, teleport the player, wait until the memory expires and at least one full aggro→engage→patrol cycle completes, then assert patrol.

Key insight to encode: the memory re-triggers aggro (the player is in the system) until it expires; after expiration, since the player is behind the cone, patrol is sticky.

Timing: firing at F. The aggro assertion is at F+100 (mode is aggro — could have aggros earlier at F+50, no problem). The memory expires at F+5000. Worst case: a re-aggro right before expiration (patrol at F+4950, memory 4850ms old ≤ 5000 → aggro at F+4950… no wait, memory age at F+4950 = 4850ms, fresh → aggro at F+4950). Engage at F+5950 → out of range → patrol at F+5950+50. So by F+6100 it's patrol. The current fakeNow after the aggro assert is F+100. advance(6200) → F+6300 > F+6100. Safe. To be generous, use 6500.

